<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uqair</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uqair is a historic port on the Gulf coast of eastern Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, in the al-Ahsa region. For centuries it served as the harbour of the al-Ahsa oasis, and its fort and customs buildings survive. Some scholars have placed ancient Gerrha near it, and in 1922 it hosted the conference that fixed the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> with Kuwait and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uqair.jpg" alt="Uqair" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: صحيفة سبق · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%A1_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%B1_%D9%81%D9%8A_%D9%85%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%82%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B4%D8%B1%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%A9_-_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%85%D9%84%D9%83%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A8%D9%8A%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A9.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
